sable poll is 81 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Marie Gluesenkamp Perez (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Washington's 3rd District pairs a slightly Republican-leaning electorate with an incumbent Democrat who has twice proven she can win it. Marie Gluesenkamp Perez has raised more than $6.2 million to John Braun's $2.2 million and holds a cash-on-hand edge, though outside spending has so far been minimal. Expert raters are split, with several calling the race a Tossup and others Likely or Lean Democratic.\n\nThe warning sign is the August top-two primary, where the incumbent finished second and a liberal rival declined to endorse her, raising questions about Democratic consolidation. Prediction markets nonetheless price her win probability near 90 percent, and the most recent independent poll from July showed her ahead. The forecast gives her a clear but not comfortable edge, with uncertainty widened by sparse and dated polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8833, "margin": 7.32}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8392, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8323, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8357, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8044, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8079, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8641, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8353, "margin": 6.0}]}